import json, pathlib, hashlib, html
p=pathlib.Path('/tmp/asterion-stage18-independent-review')
a=json.load(open(p/'results.json'));b=json.load(open(p/'initial-focus-results.json'));c=json.load(open(p/'final-flow-results.json'))
rows=''.join(f'<tr><td>{html.escape(x["name"])}</td><td>{"Pass" if x["passed"] else "Fail"}</td></tr>' for x in a['checks'])
shots=[('final-after-merge-1440.png','Final1440px: after merge, the existing quote is visible without an additional action.'),('final-after-merge-390.png','Final390px: price, duration, separate-formation wording and commission action fit without horizontal overflow.'),('merge390-initial-0orders.png','Initial narrow chooser with zero orders: heading visible, selector focused; outcomes remain readable.'),('chooser-1280-0orders-result.png','Disabled merge remains inspectable; survivor, movement and historical provenance are explicit.'),('actual40-1440-after-merge.png','Earlier phase: inspector remained at the orbit row, leaving the shortcut above the viewport. Corrected by the final focus/scroll follow-up.')]
figures=''.join(f'<figure><a href="{fn}"><img loading="lazy" src="{fn}" alt="{html.escape(caption)}"></a><figcaption>{html.escape(caption)}</figcaption></figure>' for fn,caption in shots)
source_rows=''.join(f'<tr><td>{html.escape(k)}</td><td><code>{v}</code></td></tr>' for k,v in c['sources'].items())
doc=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Stage18 independent reinforcement UI review</title><style>body{{margin:0;background:#0b1520;color:#d5e2e8;font:16px/1.65 system-ui}}main{{max-width:1060px;margin:auto;padding:40px 24px}}h1,h2{{font-weight:500;line-height:1.25;color:#d8e8dd}}h1{{font-size:36px}}h2{{margin-top:36px;font-size:23px}}a{{color:#8ed9c9}}.lede{{font-size:21px}}.note{{padding:20px;border-left:3px solid #87cdb8;background:#152833}}table{{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px}}th,td{{padding:10px 12px;border:1px solid #304550;text-align:left;vertical-align:top}}code{{font-size:11px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}}figure{{margin:28px 0}}img{{max-width:100%;max-height:800px;border:1px solid #3b5966;display:block}}figcaption{{font-size:14px;color:#a9c0ca;margin-top:8px}}.small{{font-size:13px;color:#98b0be}}</style><main><p class="small">Asterion Reach · Stage18 candidate · independent review of UI written by the other authors</p><h1>Explicit reinforcement, without hidden automation</h1><p class="lede">Accepted after one narrow flow correction. Ordinary command results remain exact, the next commission is visible after merging, and disabled choices stay readable.</p><p>The reviewer authored the pure projection module but did not author the UI, styling or main integration reviewed here. The browser ran at <code>{a['url']}</code>; this development candidate still displayed version0.17.0. This report does not claim a separate frozen-production browser run.</p><div class="note"><strong>Actual WATCH40:</strong> merge f47 ← f49, then commission a Vanguard at Solace. Exactly2orders,25credits and28minerals. f47 survives held with2ships,68hull and1move. The new queue has26work at30production and creates a separate fleet. At1440/1280/390, both paid UI commands match handwritten ordinary commands; initial acceptance also matches reload and the next complete turn.</div><h2>Evidence and limits</h2><p>The original completed campaign file was read unchanged from <code>docs/watch-playtest/checkpoints/cycle40.json</code> (SHA256 <code>{a['input']['sha256']}</code>). Fresh isolated browser contexts were used. The original WATCH files/profile were never modified. Synthetic chooser cases are explicitly separate from the human campaign; this is not a new balance cohort.</p><p>Eight initial cases passed, covering three actual-save viewport runs; a one-order chooser/merge; zero-order chooser at1280/390; a finished campaign; and a single legal partner behind an over-cap candidate. Own same-class/local filtering excludes foreign, remote and scout formations. Keyboard opening, selector changes, focus trapping, Escape restoration, readable disabled outcomes, escaped names, movement/route/Hold/lead/history explanations and viewport containment were checked.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Initial case</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody>{rows}</tbody></table><h2>Correction and source phases</h2><p>The first phase found that selecting/merging from the orbit list left the commission shortcut offscreen despite its improved placement after colony production. At1440 its button was above the viewport (y−58.9); at1280 y−108.9; at390 it was below the viewport (y1035.7). Merely reducing paid clicks did not make the next action discoverable.</p><p>The root author changed only post-merge UI focus: when the survivor has an enabled quote at the inspected owned yard, reveal/focus the existing commission panel; otherwise retain surviving-row focus. Three targeted follow-ups passed. The action is now fully visible at1440(y429–470),1280(y379–420),390(y446–487). Tab then Enter commissions exactly one ship, with exact ordinary-command state and reload equality. No duplicate paid action was added.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Phase</th><th>Scope</th><th>main.js SHA256</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Initial acceptance</td><td>8cases; full command/next-turn checks at3widths</td><td><code>{a['sourcesBefore']['src/main.js']}</code></td></tr><tr><td>Immediate opening</td><td>2narrow checks at10/0orders; heading visible, scrollTop0, selector focused</td><td><code>{b['mainSha256']}</code></td></tr><tr><td>Final correction</td><td>3targeted actual40 merge→visible quote→keyboard commission/reload checks</td><td><code>{c['sources']['src/main.js']}</code></td></tr></tbody></table><p class="small">Each run verified its source fingerprints were stable. Only main.js changed between initial acceptance and the final targeted follow-up. Earlier cases are not represented as rerun against the final hash. Root's broader production tests are separate evidence.</p><h2>Visual inspection</h2>{figures}<h2>Raw records and scripts</h2><p><a href="results.json">Initial eight-case record</a> · <a href="initial-focus-results.json">Two immediate-focus checks</a> · <a href="final-flow-results.json">Final three-width follow-up</a> · <a href="review.mjs">Initial browser driver</a> · <a href="initial-focus.mjs">Initial-focus driver</a> · <a href="final-flow.mjs">Final flow driver</a>. These measured drivers reference the recorded local worktree/browser paths; they were not modified after measurement.</p><p>Pure module commit <code>a76c341</code>; UI module/style commit <code>44c2591</code>. Main integration was uncommitted during review and is identified by exact content hashes.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Final inspected source</th><th>SHA256</th></tr></thead><tbody>{source_rows}</tbody></table><p class="small">No source changes or campaign mutations outside the isolated browser copies were performed by this review.</p></main></html>'''
(p/'index.html').write_text(doc)
manifest={'artifactHashes':{f.name:hashlib.sha256(f.read_bytes()).hexdigest() for f in sorted(p.iterdir()) if f.is_file() and f.name!='manifest.json'},'initialCases':8,'initialFocusCases':2,'finalFollowupCases':3,'finalMainSha256':c['sources']['src/main.js'],'sourceInputSha256':a['input']['sha256'],'acceptance':'Pass; prior offscreen commission issue fixed and targeted final flow verified.'}
